# ── ICE fetch state — deliberately NOT committed ─────────────────────────────
# The fetcher writes these as it runs. They stay on the runner and die with it:
#
#   stock_report_hits.json    the exact second-of-day ICE published each report.
#                             That is an observed timing edge, and it is private
#                             to 619 by design. It only exists to let a run skip
#                             ahead in the sweep — an optimisation that saves
#                             billed minutes, which is precisely what 620 does
#                             not spend. Sweeping blind here costs nothing.
#   stock_report_cursor.json  where a sweep got to; carries publish-time hints.
#   ice_run_stats.json        per-run request/throttle diagnostics.
#   state/ice_block_state.json  edge-triggered block notification state.
#
# Consequence, accepted deliberately: each 620 run sweeps from scratch and takes
# longer in wall-clock. Free compute is the whole point of running it here.
fetch/scraper/sources/ice_certified_stocks/stock_report_hits.json
fetch/scraper/sources/ice_certified_stocks/stock_report_cursor.json
fetch/scraper/sources/ice_certified_stocks/ice_run_stats.json
fetch/state/
_stage/
